--- AGENT RESPONSE (FULL) ---
Length: 4166 chars
Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
I can help — first a quick check and then a clear plan to compute CAC and LTV and build the finance narrative.

1) Quick consistency check
- You told me: cash = $5.2M, runway = 30 months, burn = $72K/month.
- 5.2M ÷ 30 months = ~$173K/month, not $72K. Conversely, 5.2M ÷ $72K ≈ 72 months.
Please confirm which two of these three values are correct (cash, runway, burn), and how you define “burn” (net cash burn after revenue, or operating cash outflow excluding revenue?). I’ll use the corrected values in the narrative.

2) Data I need from you (minimum to calculate CAC & LTV)
- Sales & Marketing spend for the period you want to measure (e.g., last quarter or last 12 months) — include direct S&M and any customer-acquisition commissions.
- Number of new customers acquired in that same period.
- Total active customers (or number of paying accounts) now.
- Gross margin on revenue (or cost of goods sold %).
- Customer churn rate (monthly or annual) OR average customer lifetime if you already have it.
If you don’t have churn, I can work from cohort data or industry defaults but I’ll flag assumptions.

3) Formulas and definitions (so the finance narrative is precise)
- CAC = Total Sales & Marketing Spend (period) ÷ Number of New Customers Acquired (same period)
- ARPU (monthly) = Monthly Revenue ÷ Total Active Customers
- LTV (simple cohort formula) = (ARPU × Gross Margin %) ÷ Churn Rate (if churn is monthly)
  - Equivalent: LTV = ARPU × Gross Margin × Average Customer Lifetime
- Payback Period (months) = CAC ÷ (ARPU × Gross Margin)
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV ÷ CAC
Notes: Use monthly ARPU and monthly churn for the month-based formula. If you only have annual churn, use annual equivalents.

4) Benchmarks and targets to include in the narrative
- Healthy LTV/CAC target: ≥ 3x (many VCs/finance teams use ≥ 3)
- Payback period target: ≤ 12 months (best if ≤ 6–12 months depending on growth mode)
- CAC as % of new ARR or as percentage of revenue growth budget — show sensitivity (if CAC rises, how many months to payback, impact on cash runway).

5) Illustrative examples (so you see the calculation)
Assumptions (example):
- Revenue last quarter = $670K → monthly revenue ≈ $223.3K
- Suppose total customers = 800 → monthly ARPU = 223,333 ÷ 800 = $279
- Suppose gross margin = 75% and monthly churn = 2%
- Suppose S&M spend last quarter = $200K and new customers that quarter = 100

Then:
- CAC = $200,000 ÷ 100 = $2,000
- LTV = (ARPU × GM) ÷ churn = (279 × 0.75) ÷ 0.02 = 209.25 ÷ 0.02 = $10,462
- LTV/CAC ≈ 10,462 ÷ 2,000 = 5.23 (strong)
- Payback months = CAC ÷ (ARPU × GM) = 2,000 ÷ 209.25 ≈ 9.6 months

I can produce 2–3 sensitivity scenarios (best / base / worst) by varying churn, gross margin, and S&M efficiency for your slide or memo.

6) How this ties to runway and finance narrative
- Show how increased S&M (to accelerate growth) affects cash runway: incremental monthly cash spend = planned incremental S&M spend minus incremental gross profit from new customers (use payback).
- If LTV/CAC < 3 or payback > 12 months, argue for conserving cash or improving funnel efficiency before scaling S&M.
- If LTV/CAC is healthy and payback short, support investing a portion of cash into S&M to increase growth, and show projected ARR growth scenarios and their runway impacts.
- Always include sensitivity tables: e.g., if CAC increases 20% or churn increases 1pp, what happens to payback and runway.

7) Next step — what I can do now
Option A — If you provide the data items I listed (S&M spend, new customers, total customers, gross margin, churn, and confirm cash/runway/burn), I will:
- Calculate CAC, ARPU, LTV, LTV/CAC, payback
- Produce 3 scenarios (base / optimistic / conservative)
- Draft a short finance narrative you can paste into internal materials (key assumptions, results, recommendations, and suggested S&M budget tied to runway)

Option B — If you want me to proceed using reasonable industry assumptions, tell me which assumptions you prefer (conservative/typical/aggressive) and I’ll produce the numbers and narrative.

Which option do you want? If Option A, please paste the missing data and confirm the runway/burn values.

