I can help — but first a quick flag: the numbers you gave don’t line up. At $5.2M cash and a $72K/month burn, runway = 5.2M / 72K ≈ 72 months (not 30). Conversely, for 30 months runway your net burn would be ≈ $173K/month. Which of these is correct (burn = $72K or runway = 30 months)? Also tell me whether “burn” is net burn after revenue or gross operating cash burn.

What I can do next
- Explain the formulas and the data you need to compute CAC and LTV precisely.
- Show example calculations and a sensitivity table (several plausible scenarios) so you can use those in the finance narrative.
