What I need from you to compute CAC and LTV (and what they mean)
- CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) = (total sales + marketing spend in period) / (number of new customers acquired in that same period).
  - Inputs needed: S&M spend (ads, sales comp & commissions, agency fees, marketing ops) for the period you want to measure (monthly/quarterly/annual) and # of new customers acquired in that period.

- LTV (Customer Lifetime Value) — common SaaS formula:
  - LTV = ARPA_monthly * Gross Margin % * (1 / monthly churn rate)
  - ARPA_monthly = revenue per month per active customer (Total revenue in period / # active customers / months in period)
