Key metrics and formulas
- Monthly revenue (Rmonth) = last quarter revenue / 3. (You gave $670K → Rmonth = $670,000 / 3 = $223,333.)
- ARPU (monthly) = Rmonth / number of active customers.
- Gross contribution per customer (monthly) = ARPU * Gross Margin.
- Average customer lifetime (months) = 1 / monthly churn rate.
- LTV (per customer) = ARPU * Gross Margin * (1 / monthly churn).
  (Equivalent: LTV = monthly gross contribution * avg lifetime.)
- CAC = Total Sales & Marketing spend in a period / number of customers acquired in that period.
- LTV : CAC ratio = LTV / CAC (target > 3x for healthy SaaS; > 3–4 is common).
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (ARPU * Gross Margin).

Information I need from you to calculate exact CAC and LTV
- Current number of active customers (or MRR per customer breakdown)
- Monthly or quarterly S&M spend (or S&M as a % of revenue)
- New customers acquired per month (or for the quarter)
